== the SCOPE rule, executed on the fabricated directory ==
The round this rule binds is derived from the file NAMES, so a round
that declares no stdout anywhere cannot leave the scope by declaring
nothing. Both directions are driven here on a fabricated directory
rather than on this one, because this directory satisfies the old
reading and the new one alike and cannot tell them apart.

cwd       <repo>
command   python -c "import sys; sys.stdout.reconfigure(newline=chr(10)); import importlib.util as u; s=u.spec_from_file_location('r','backend/tests/evidence/evidence_rules.py'); m=u.module_from_spec(s); s.loader.exec_module(m); print('adopting round clean ->', m.scope_problems(m.FABRICATED_DIRECTORY)); print('round that opted out ->', sorted(n for n,_ in m.scope_problems(m.FABRICATED_DIRECTORY_OPTED_OUT)))"
adopting round clean -> []
round that opted out -> ['r3-mutation-controls.txt', 'r3-suites.txt']
scope rc=0

